# One-Line Imports

When adding or editing imports:

- Keep each import statement on a single line whenever possible.
- Avoid multiline named import blocks.
- If a formatter or linter forces multiline imports, split into additional single-line import statements instead of using a multiline block.
- Preserve existing import ordering conventions in the file.
- Apply this rule on all code edits where imports are touched.

## Preferred pattern

Use:

```typescript
import React from "react";
import { useEffect, useMemo, useRef, useState, useCallback } from "react";
import { Button } from "@/components/Button";
```

Avoid:

```typescript
import React, {
  useEffect,
  useMemo,
  useRef,
  useState,
  useCallback,
} from "react";
```

## Notes

- Do not change runtime behavior while reformatting imports.
- If a path alias or style rule prevents combining imports, add a new import line rather than using multiline braces.
